WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:23.599
Lee Harvey Oswald – the Man who Killed a
President

00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:36.879
On November 22, 1963, 24 year old Lee Harvey
Oswald fired the shot that would change history.

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:41.150
As crowds cheered on Dealey Plaza, the former
Marine sharpshooter put a bullet through the

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.170
head of America’s telegenic young President.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.430
It was the first successful assassination
of a US president in 62 years.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:53.440
But Oswald didn’t live long enough to celebrate
his grim achievement.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:58.220
Not two days later, Oswald would be dead too,
killed by an assassin’s bullet while in

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.220
police custody.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.309
It’s a story you’ve doubtless heard many
times before.

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:08.220
But it’s also only a fragment, a single
chapter in the vast, messy novel of Lee Harvey

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.860
Oswald’s life.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:14.760
Born in 1939 to a New Orleans widow, Oswald
was a man who tried his best to live a life

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.760
of adventure.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.270
He enlisted in the Marines, defected to the
Soviet Union, flirted with spies in Mexico

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.270
City.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:26.500
But it was a single shot fired in Dallas that
would cement his place in history.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:35.560
Join us today as we explore the life of America’s
most notorious assassin.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.930
The Wanderer
When Lee Harvey Oswald first opened his eyes

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:46.000
on October 18, 1939, he had no way of knowing
he’d just been born into a world paralyzed

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.060
by tragedy.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.890
Not two months earlier, the boy’s father,
Robert Oswald Snr., had died of a heart attack,

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:55.110
leaving his heavily pregnant wife Marguerite
to look after their two sons.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:02:00.600
These dire circumstances may explain the dislocated
early life baby Lee experienced.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.450
In 1942, Marguerite sent Lee’s older brothers
away to boarding schools.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.710
She tried to drop Lee at a local orphanage,
but was told he was too young.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.039
Undeterred, she simply waited a year and then
had him admitted.

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:15.300
And so began the incredibly depressing childhood
of Lee Harvey Oswald.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.040
For the next few years, young Lee bounced
between orphanages, relatives’ homes, apartments

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:25.110
Marguerite managed to briefly find and just
as quickly lose… you name it.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:30.100
In 1952, when the boy was 12, Marguerite even
took him with her all the way across the country,

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.820
as far from the bayous and old colonial piles
of Louisiana as she could.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.840
All the way to New York City.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.300
But if Ma Oswald was expecting the streets
in the Bronx to be paved with gold, she soon

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.110
got a dose of harsh, cold reality.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.970
Life in New York City was hard.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:50.920
Marguerite took a job at a dress shop, but
it required her to work backbreaking hours,

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.500
hours in which her young son was left to his
own devices.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:59.470
As a consequence, Lee Harvey Oswald entered
his teenage years lonely and rootless, spending

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:04.280
long, listless days kicking his heels at the
Bronx Zoo, or aimlessly riding the subway.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.710
Technically, he was supposed to be in school,
a fact that did not go unnoticed by the truant

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:11.930
officer who picked him up one day in 1953.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:17.060
By this point, 13-year old Lee had moved over
20 times in his short life, usually after

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.760
Marguerite’s latest job or latest relationship
blew up in her face.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.540
The boy was surly, withdrawn.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:24.870
Prone to violence.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.700
He sometimes threatened others with a pocket
knife.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:32.570
So rather than just caution this wayward child,
the truant officer sent him to a psychiatric

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:33.570
facility.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:37.940
There, Lee was found to suffer from neglect,
but no actual mental illness.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:43.150
He was just another directionless kid with
too much time on his hands and no-one to love

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.150
him.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:48.180
But while the love situation wouldn’t change,
Lee’s life was about to get a whole lot

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.270
of direction.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:56.040
On June 19, 1953, Julius and Ethel Rosenberg
were executed by electric chair at New York’s

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:59.880
Sing Sing Prison for handing US secrets to
the Soviets.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.930
The execution galvanized New York’s leftists,
who campaigned across the city in the weeks

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.760
leading up, handing out leaflets.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:11.530
One of these leaflets made its way into the
hands of teenage Lee Harvey Oswald.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:15.280
For the first time in his life, the boy encountered
socialism.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:20.500
As the Rosenbergs’ bodies were quietly buried,
Lee started reading books on socialist thought.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.720
It was an obsession that survived even his
next major move.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:30.790
In 1954, Marguerite abandoned New York City,
dragging her son back to New Orleans and an

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.750
apartment on Exchange Alley in the French
Quarter.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.210
Today, the French Quarter is famous as a tourist
hotspot.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:42.470
In 1954, though, Exchange Alley was the seediest
part of a seedy city, crawling with pimps,

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.180
prostitutes, and mobsters.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:47.639
Lee even had a connection to the local mafia,
via his uncle, Charles Murret.

00:04:47.639 --> 00:04:50.889
It was a world Lee couldn’t wait to escape
from.

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:55.880
In 1955, the teenager applied to the Marines,
lying about his age, but was found out and

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:56.880
rejected.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.630
A year later, aged 17, he tried again.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:00.740
This time, he got in.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:05.810
In 1956, Lee Harvey Oswald officially became
a member of the United States Marine Corps.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:09.930
He likely hoped it would be the start of a
new chapter in his life, a way to escape his

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:10.930
problems.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:15.940
But when your problems are as deep rooted
as Lee Harvey Oswald’s were, escaping them

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:20.660
is easier said than done.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:26.570
Defection
So, here’s the thing about joining the Marines

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:30.220
if what you really need is a place to settle
and call home.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.449
That ain’t gonna happen.

00:05:32.449 --> 00:05:36.820
No sooner was his training complete than Lee
Harvey Oswald was shipped off to Japan, before

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:39.870
being shipped off to the Philippines, and
then back to the US.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:43.150
Yep, it was his wayward childhood all over
again.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:46.380
Only now the weapons he carried were bigger
than just a pocket knife.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:50.110
While in the Marines, Oswald managed to gain
certification as a sharpshooter.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:54.550
He also developed an interest in banned weapons,
an interest that got him in a lot of trouble

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:58.270
when his forbidden pistol accidentally discharged
and wounded him.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:01.650
The discovery of Oswald’s pistol led him
to be court martialed, which led him to be

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:05.220
court martialed again when he got angry and
attacked the sergeant who was court martialing

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.220
him.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.530
The sorry debacle ended with Oswald spending
time in the brig.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:10.540
When he emerged, he was more bitter than ever.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:14.360
That’s not to say Oswald’s time in the
Marines was all a disaster.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:17.580
The young man continued to study Marxism,
and learned Russian.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.880
He even began preaching about Marx’s ideas
to his fellow Marines.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:25.250
Note to any drill sergeants out there: if
one of your marines suddenly starts being

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:30.699
all pro-Soviet in the middle of the Cold War,
it’s totally OK to tell the FBI, guys!

00:06:30.699 --> 00:06:35.250
That goes double if you happen to be living
in 1959.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:39.470
On January 1 that year, Fidel Castro overthrew
the Cuban government and installed the first

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:42.330
Communist dictatorship in the Americas.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:45.310
We don’t know precisely how Oswald reacted
to this news.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:49.300
But we do know he intensified his efforts
with his Russian.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.190
By now, it was clear a plan was forming in
the young marine’s mind.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:55.580
A plan that would help him escape his problems
once and for all.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:07:00.270
On September 11, 1959, Oswald got a hardship
discharge from the Marines.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:04.760
Just nine days later, he boarded a boat to
Europe, where he intended to apply to a Swiss

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:05.760
college.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:06.760
He never made it.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:09.400
The moment Oswald reached England, he boarded
a flight to Helsinki.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.790
There, he applied for and soon got a Russian
tourist visa.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:18.389
On October 16, 1959, Lee Harvey Oswald officially
crossed into the Soviet Union.

00:07:18.389 --> 00:07:22.290
Barely had the ink dried on his entry stamp
then he declared to his Russian guide that

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.430
he wanted to defect.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:27.669
Thanks to spy movies, we tend to imagine the
Soviet authorities were always on the lookout

00:07:27.669 --> 00:07:29.990
for Americans willing to go Red.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.590
In reality, it didn’t quite work like that.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:34.400
Oswald wrote to the Kremlin, telling them
he wanted to defect.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:38.940
The Kremlin took one look at his application
and were all like “nahhhhh”.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:41.050
The rejection hit Oswald hard.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:46.250
On October 21, the day his visa ran out, he
slit one of his wrists in his hotel bathtub.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:49.259
In hospital, Oswald was again interviewed
by the KGB.

00:07:49.259 --> 00:07:52.259
Again, they decided he wasn’t defector material.

00:07:52.259 --> 00:07:54.820
So Oswald forced their hands.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:59.669
On October 31, the newly-discharged Oswald
stormed into the US embassy in Moscow and

00:07:59.669 --> 00:08:02.130
declared he was going to surrender his citizenship.

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:06.820
Worse, he was going to tell the Kremlin everything
he knew about US radar codes.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:11.350
In the minor storm that followed, the Kremlin
reluctantly agreed to reopen his case.

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:16.640
On January 4, 1960, they finally approved
Oswald to defect to the Soviet Union.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.270
When he got the news, Oswald must have felt
like partying.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:20.970
Finally, it had happened.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:26.630
He’d found a way to escape his overbearing
mother, to escape his wandering, American

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:27.630
life.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:29.110
Now he’d have a place in this world at last.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.509
A home to call his own.

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:31.820
A home known as…

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:32.820
Belarus?

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:33.820
Wait, what?

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:39.179
On a freezing cold January day, Lee Harvey
Oswald was ordered away from glamorous Moscow

00:08:39.179 --> 00:08:43.649
to the grim, gray streets of the Belarusian
capital, Minsk.

00:08:43.649 --> 00:08:51.509
Rather than a fresh new start, the move would
soon turn out to be a horrendous mistake.

00:08:51.509 --> 00:08:56.931
A Lonely Exile
If you’ve never been to Minsk – and we

00:08:56.931 --> 00:09:01.119
mean it with all sincerity when we say “lucky
you” – you should know it’s a city that

00:09:01.119 --> 00:09:03.110
will never win any tourist awards.

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:09.600
Rebuilt in a cold, Stalinist style following
its total destruction in WWII, Minsk is Kiev

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:14.529
without the charm, Chisinau without the nightlife,
Warsaw without the edge.

00:09:14.529 --> 00:09:18.480
Stepping off the train there in the dead of
winter in 1960 must have felt only slightly

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:22.679
less depressing than stepping off the Styx
River into the Underworld.

00:09:22.679 --> 00:09:26.279
Still, Oswald’s new life wasn’t without
a certain charm.

00:09:26.279 --> 00:09:29.730
Minsk in 1960 wasn’t a city that was used
to seeing Americans.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.929
The moment Oswald arrived, he was treated
as a celebrity.

00:09:32.929 --> 00:09:37.610
Not only that, the Kremlin gave him a luxury
apartment – luxury by USSR standards – and

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.889
a plush job making radios.

00:09:39.889 --> 00:09:44.420
With all this adulation, it was kind of easy
for Oswald to forget what a precarious position

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:45.790
he’d put himself in.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:49.550
Kind of easy to pretend his marine discharge
being downgraded to “undesirable” might

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:51.399
not cause him problems in the future.

00:09:51.399 --> 00:09:55.760
It was only after about 6 months, when locals
were used to him and the novelty of defection

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:00.769
had worn off, that Oswald realized he was
now living in a boring foreign city with nothing

00:10:00.769 --> 00:10:01.769
to do.

00:10:01.769 --> 00:10:04.560
It probably didn’t help that the KGB was
openly monitoring him.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:08.790
Oswald’s entire apartment was bugged, informants
watched his every move.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:12.920
By February, 1961, Oswald was writing in his
dairy “(my) work is drab.

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.480
The money I get has nowhere to be spent.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:20.720
As my Russian improves, I become increasingly
conscious of just what sort of a society I

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.720
live in.”

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:27.209
Barely a year after he first arrived in Minsk,
Oswald began petitioning the US and USSR to

00:10:27.209 --> 00:10:28.689
let him return to America.

00:10:28.689 --> 00:10:32.730
But the America that existed now was not the
same one Oswald had left.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:36.959
The previous November, a telegenic young man
had narrowly squeaked home to victory in the

00:10:36.959 --> 00:10:38.350
US presidential election.

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:42.379
Known as John F Kennedy, he was the youngest
elected president in American history.

00:10:42.379 --> 00:10:46.220
Not that JFK preyed much on Oswald’s mind
that year.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:49.940
No sooner had he decided to leave Minsk than
he found a reason to stay.

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:55.930
In mid-March, 1961, Oswald met Marina Prusakova
by chance at a trade union dance.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:57.790
Well, it was supposedly by chance.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:02.310
Marina’s uncle worked for Soviet intelligence,
and it’s long been suspected he engineered

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:03.800
Marina’s meeting with the American.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:09.670
Regardless, the two hit it off and, a mere
six weeks later, on April 30, 1961, they married.

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:15.890
Barely nine months later, on February 15,
1962, Marina Oswald gave birth to their daughter,

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:16.890
June.

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:21.980
It was at this time that Lee Harvey Oswald
began taking his return to the USA very seriously.

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:25.810
Aware that finding work in America with an
undesirable discharge hanging over him would

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:28.660
be difficult, Oswald came up with a desperate
plan.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:33.300
He wrote directly to Secretary of the Navy,
John Connally, asking for his discharge to

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:34.379
be scrubbed.

00:11:34.379 --> 00:11:39.000
In return, he merely got a glossy leaflet
asking him to support Connally for Governor

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.000
of Texas.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.819
It was more than just a slap in the face.

00:11:41.819 --> 00:11:46.459
To Oswald’s mind, it was like Connally had
personally urinated on him and then seduced

00:11:46.459 --> 00:11:47.459
his mother.

00:11:47.459 --> 00:11:52.139
From that moment on, Oswald began nursing
a grudge against Connally that would soon

00:11:52.139 --> 00:11:55.059
grow to murderous proportions.

00:11:55.059 --> 00:11:58.519
Undesirable discharge or not, though, the
Oswald family’s petition to return to the

00:11:58.519 --> 00:12:00.839
USA was gaining steam.

00:12:00.839 --> 00:12:04.940
It turned out Oswald never had surrendered
his American citizenship, despite threatening

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.649
to do so back in Moscow.

00:12:06.649 --> 00:12:10.110
When this came to light, there was little
the Americans or Soviets could realistically

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:12.249
do to keep the family in Minsk.

00:12:12.249 --> 00:12:16.949
On June 2, 1962, Oswald, Marina, and their
baby daughter June all received permission

00:12:16.949 --> 00:12:18.679
to return to the US.

00:12:18.679 --> 00:12:22.509
They headed straight for Fort Worth, Texas,
where they moved in with one of Oswald’s

00:12:22.509 --> 00:12:23.509
brothers.

00:12:23.509 --> 00:12:26.999
Just like that, Oswald’s career as a professional
defector was over.

00:12:26.999 --> 00:12:29.100
He was now back in the land of the Free.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:13:29.949
And it wouldn’t be long before Oswald was
using those freedoms to buy himself

00:13:29.949 --> 00:13:32.389
a gun.

00:13:32.389 --> 00:14:07.610
Dreams of Cuba
So, given Oswald’s past, you’re probably

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:12.569
expecting to hear how his return to America
was marked by the Feds dragging him off for

00:14:12.569 --> 00:14:14.230
a lengthy interrogation.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:15.779
Not quite.

00:14:15.779 --> 00:14:19.930
While the FBI did check in with Oswald, the
CIA didn’t even bother to send anyone out

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:20.930
to talk to him.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:25.369
Unless you believe the theories that say the
CIA did debrief Oswald, but then destroyed

00:14:25.369 --> 00:14:28.639
the evidence after JFK got shot to cover their
tracks.

00:14:28.639 --> 00:14:33.470
Either way, come summer, 1962, Oswald was
living in Texas, looking for a job.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.699
It was not a happy search.

00:14:35.699 --> 00:14:41.129
Remember how we said his undesirable discharge
might be a massive deal when looking for employment?

00:14:41.129 --> 00:14:43.920
Well it turned out to absolutely be a massive
deal.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:48.799
So many places turned Oswald down after learning
about his unhappy break with the Marines.

00:14:48.799 --> 00:14:53.389
According to people who knew him, Oswald responded
to these setbacks by blaming the man who had

00:14:53.389 --> 00:14:56.610
refused to scrub his discharge: John Connally.

00:14:56.610 --> 00:15:00.279
But not even an undesirably discharged defector
is completely unemployable.

00:15:00.279 --> 00:15:05.850
In October, 1962, a Minsk émigré friend
of Marina finally got Oswald a job in Dallas.

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:19.359
But there was something else that had caught
Oswald’s magpie mind by this time: Cuba.

00:15:19.359 --> 00:15:22.529
That fall, Oswald began to obsess over Castro’s
new Cuba.

00:15:22.529 --> 00:15:27.109
He started to tell people Kennedy was a terrible
president for authorizing the 1961 Bay of

00:15:27.109 --> 00:15:30.799
Pigs invasion – a bungled attempt to overthrow
Castro.

00:15:30.799 --> 00:15:36.720
It was at a Dallas party in February, 1963
that Oswald aired these views to one Volkmar

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:37.720
Schmidt.

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:42.339
Schmidt snorted and told Oswald he should
be far more angry at Edwin Walker.

00:15:42.339 --> 00:15:47.419
An ultrarightist, Walker had been forced to
retire his post as a general for teaching

00:15:47.419 --> 00:15:49.329
his soldiers fascist ideas.

00:15:49.329 --> 00:15:52.139
Something about Walker’s story caught Oswald’s
imagination.

00:15:52.139 --> 00:15:54.299
He began to stalk the former general.

00:15:54.299 --> 00:15:57.889
Not long after, he ordered a pistol and a
rifle through the mail.

00:15:57.889 --> 00:16:01.899
On April 10, 1963, Marina was home late at
night when Oswald came bursting through the

00:16:01.899 --> 00:16:05.359
door, white as a sheet, babbling that he’d
shot him.

00:16:05.359 --> 00:16:07.059
“Him” was Edwin Walker.

00:16:07.059 --> 00:16:10.930
Less than an hour earlier, a single bullet
had come through Walker’s window, just missing

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.019
the ex-general.

00:16:12.019 --> 00:16:16.649
The shot had been fired by Oswald, who’d
buried the rifle and fled the scene, convinced

00:16:16.649 --> 00:16:17.759
he’d killed Walker.

00:16:17.759 --> 00:16:22.170
It was only when Marina turned on the radio
that Oswald realized he’d missed.

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:25.430
Not two weeks later, Oswald vanished from
Texas.

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:30.679
This is where we get into the really mysterious
part of Lee Harvey Oswald’s life.

00:16:30.679 --> 00:16:35.949
We know he eventually resurfaced in New Orleans,
but the timeline of what he did there is all

00:16:35.949 --> 00:16:36.949
confused.

00:16:36.949 --> 00:16:41.149
Proponents of the theory that the mafia killed
Kennedy believe Oswald spent his time in New

00:16:41.149 --> 00:16:46.029
Orleans getting connected to the mob via his
uncle, Charles Murret.

00:16:46.029 --> 00:16:49.949
Whether or not that’s the case, we do know
he took a minor job at a coffee company, and

00:16:49.949 --> 00:16:52.519
sent for Marina and June to join him.

00:16:52.519 --> 00:16:55.019
But all this was just a sideshow.

00:16:55.019 --> 00:16:58.430
Oswald’s real interest in New Orleans was
Cuba.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:03.779
That May, 1963, Oswald founded a pro-Castro
group, handing out leaflets in the street,

00:17:03.779 --> 00:17:05.949
trying – and failing – to recruit new
members.

00:17:05.949 --> 00:17:08.839
Yet he seems to have been playing some sort
of game.

00:17:08.839 --> 00:17:12.530
In August, Oswald approached an anti-Castro
group and offered his services.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.230
The group turned him away.

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:17.000
Still, Cuba remained a powerful draw in the
young man’s mind.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:20.030
He appeared on local radio twice to defend
the Castro regime.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:25.070
In September, he told Marina he was planning
to hijack a plane and fly it to Havana.

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:28.740
Eventually, this strange dream completely
consumed the dreamer.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:33.180
On September 25, Oswald vanished from New
Orleans, just as suddenly as he vanished from

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:34.180
Dallas.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:36.290
His exact movements that night are unknown.

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:41.100
Years later, an anti-Castro activist in Dallas
would recall a man named “Leon Oswald”

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:45.680
showing up on his doorstep, asking for money
to help the guerilla war against Castro.

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:47.050
The activist refused.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:50.990
Regardless, we know exactly where Oswald was
by mid-morning the next day.

00:17:50.990 --> 00:17:52.700
He was on a bus bound for Mexico City.

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:58.370
And he had a plan that would make his past
defection look like a mere warm-up act.

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:04.830
City of Spies
At the height of the Cold War, there was no

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:08.490
more shadowy city in the Americas than Mexico
City.

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:10.120
Officially, Mexico was neutral.

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:15.470
Unofficially, it was a hotbed of clandestine
meetings, dangerous games, and spies gunning

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.100
to get the drop on one another.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:22.490
Into this setup for a Graham Greene novel
walked the most shadowy man of them all.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:28.040
Lee Harvey Oswald arrived in the Mexican capital
on September 27, after an all-night bus journey.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:32.280
Barley had he dumped his bag in the hotel
than he was making for the Cuban embassy.

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:34.280
Oswald had made up his mind.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:36.030
He was going to defect to Cuba.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:41.350
OK, so remember how the USSR was initially
all like “nah, dude, we don’t want you”?

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:44.240
Well, Cuba was even more like “nahhhhh.

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.040
Sorry, but nahhhhhh.”

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:50.490
Rebuffed, Oswald went to the Soviet embassy
and tried to get a transit visa through Cuba,

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:52.560
presumably hoping to defect when he landed.

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:55.700
But the Soviets were also like “nahhhh.”

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:57.130
So Oswald went back to the Cubans.

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:59.520
He literally begged them to take him.

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:00.580
But they refused.

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:02.490
Broken, Oswald left the Cuban embassy.

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:07.430
Five days later, he was on a bus back to Dallas,
his shiny new dream in tatters.

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:10.040
At least, that’s the official version.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:16.170
The unofficial version comes from reports
by CIA assets in Mexico City when Oswald arrived.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.080
They paint a very different picture.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:23.230
The spy June Cobb reported Oswald had been
spotted at a party attended by Cuban diplomats.

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:26.910
While there, he was overheard joking about
killing JFK.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:31.760
Another asset claimed to have seen Oswald
at a separate party, conversing with two Americans.

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:34.520
These two men have never been identified.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.340
Spooky stuff, eh?

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:40.540
Whether you believe the official or unofficial
versions, there’s no denying that Oswald

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:43.060
was back in Dallas by October 3.

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:47.480
Exactly two weeks later, he took a job at
the Texas School Book Depository.

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:52.720
From this point on, the story of Lee Harvey
Oswald takes on a feeling of inevitability.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:56.240
On October 20, Marina gave birth to Oswald’s
second daughter.

00:19:56.240 --> 00:20:00.870
Just three days later, Oswald clandestinely
attended a rightwing rally being held by Edwin

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:03.310
Walker – the general he’d tried to shoot.

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:06.530
On November 1, the FBI came knocking at Marina’s
door.

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:10.720
She was living with a friend after a row with
Oswald, and was surprised to discover the

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.640
Feds wanted to talk with him.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:15.280
When word reached Oswald, he became jumpy.

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:20.030
On Tuesday, November 19, a local Dallas paper
published the route the President’s motorcade

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:21.910
would take through the city on Friday.

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:25.720
Oswald noted that the car would pass right
by his place of work.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:29.780
He also noted that Governor John Connally
would be riding alongside the president.

00:20:29.780 --> 00:20:34.250
Finally, on November 21, Oswald went to the
house of the friend Marina was staying with;

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:37.820
incidentally, the same place he had left his
rifle for safekeeping.

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:40.820
That evening, he tried to make up with Marina
three times.

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.650
Each time, Marina refused.

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:46.440
Oswald wound up spending the night in the
garage, his rifle beside him.

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:53.620
And that was how things stood as the clock
ticked midnight and November 22, 1963 officially

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:54.640
began.

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:58.860
President Kennedy was on his way to Dallas,
and Oswald was just a nobody who dreamed of

00:20:58.860 --> 00:20:59.910
being a somebody.

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:11.200
In just over twelve hours, that dream would
become a nightmarish reality.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.730
The Shot that Changed the World
The morning he entered the history books,

00:21:12.730 --> 00:21:17.410
Lee Harvey Oswald woke up early, removed his
wedding ring, and left it and some money alongside

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:18.550
the sleeping Marina.

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:21.890
He wrapped his rifle in paper, and took it
with him to work on the sixth floor at the

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:23.360
Texas School Book Depository.

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:26.430
At noon, Oswald’s fellow workers clocked
off for lunch.

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:28.470
He told them he would be right with them.

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:33.160
Then he patiently waited until they’d all
filed into the elevator and left, before going

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.750
back to retrieve his rifle.

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:40.200
At 12:29pm exactly, as advertised, the presidential
motorcade swung onto Dealey Plaza.

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:44.260
As John F Kennedy waved at the crowds, the
wife of Governor John Connally leaned toward

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:47.800
the president and said:
“Mr President, you can’t say Dallas doesn’t

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:48.800
love you.”

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:52.180
Those would be the last coherent words Kennedy
would ever hear.

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:56.470
As the clock ticked over to 12:30, there was
the distant crack of a gunshot.

00:21:56.470 --> 00:22:00.440
If you watch the Kennedy footage carefully,
you can see that Governor Connally heard this

00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:01.490
first shot.

00:22:01.490 --> 00:22:03.940
He reacts, starts to turn around…

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:08.680
And then the entire, sensible world shattered
into a billion pieces.

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:10.000
There was another crack.

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:14.310
A bullet went through the President’s throat,
hit Governor Connally, causing him to slump

00:22:14.310 --> 00:22:15.310
forwards.

00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:18.520
In the car, Jackie Kennedy grabbed her husband,
asking him what was wrong.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:22.850
Up on the sixth floor of the Texas School
Book Depository, Lee Harvey Oswald took aim

00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:24.280
with his rifle again.

00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:27.620
Five seconds later came the third, final,
crack.

00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:30.940
President Kennedy’s head jerked back with
the force of the bullet.

00:22:30.940 --> 00:22:32.800
The screen faded to black.

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:36.190
The rest of that fateful afternoon you already
know.

00:22:36.190 --> 00:22:39.230
The images of panic in the streets are seared
onto our minds.

00:22:39.230 --> 00:22:43.990
The sound of Walter Cronkite’s voice, disbelievingly
telling the nation that President Kennedy

00:22:43.990 --> 00:22:44.990
is dead.

00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:50.080
You know, too, the way Oswald fled the scene,
only to shoot Officer J.D Tippit dead less

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:51.420
than an hour later.

00:22:51.420 --> 00:22:55.480
You likely remember the story of how Oswald
then tried to hide in a movie theater, only

00:22:55.480 --> 00:22:57.130
to be arrested shortly after.

00:22:57.130 --> 00:23:02.710
At midnight that same day, Oswald was booked
for assassinating the president and paraded

00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:03.800
before the press.

00:23:03.800 --> 00:23:08.800
It’s only with hindsight that we can look
at photos of that moment, and notice Jack

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:10.940
Ruby, lurking in the background.

00:23:10.940 --> 00:23:17.050
By the time the clock ticked over and November
22, 1963 receded into history, nobody on Earth

00:23:17.050 --> 00:23:18.080
had any doubt.

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:22.420
In less than 10 seconds that afternoon, a
single man had pulled a trigger and changed

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:23.420
the world.

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:25.530
The dream was over.

00:23:25.530 --> 00:23:28.170
Nothing would ever be the same again.

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:33.840
“I’m Happy that I got Him.”

00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:39.280
After the drama of the previous day, Saturday
November 23, 1963 was eerily quiet.

00:23:39.280 --> 00:23:43.180
In Dallas, Lee Harvey Oswald sat in a police
cell, protesting his innocence.

00:23:43.180 --> 00:23:48.410
Outside, a local strip club owner named Jack
Ruby hung around, asking every cop he saw

00:23:48.410 --> 00:23:51.400
what time Oswald would be transferred to another
jail.

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:54.940
The only thing of note that really happened
that day was the first broadcast of the long-running

00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:56.910
British sci-fi series Doctor Who.

00:23:56.910 --> 00:24:01.420
But we’re gonna guess maybe people in Dallas
were too preoccupied to care much about that?

00:24:01.420 --> 00:24:07.530
But if November 23 passed in stunned silence,
November 24 would be marked by the crack of

00:24:07.530 --> 00:24:08.550
another gunshot.

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:14.280
At 11:17am that morning, Dallas police led
Lee Harvey Oswald out into a waiting crowd

00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:16.560
to be transferred to another facility.

00:24:16.560 --> 00:24:20.720
No-one noticed as Jack Ruby sauntered down
the ramp towards the prisoner, murder in his

00:24:20.720 --> 00:24:21.840
eyes.

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:25.610
No-one noticed the revolver being raised,
the sudden movement.

00:24:25.610 --> 00:24:29.400
There are photos you can find of the exact
moment Oswald was shot.

00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:32.750
His mouth is wide open, his eyes bugging out
his head.

00:24:32.750 --> 00:24:37.520
The crowd of policemen look blandly at him,
as if they haven’t yet realized what is

00:24:37.520 --> 00:24:38.520
happening.

00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:40.310
Oswald collapsed into a pool of blood.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:42.950
As he was grabbed by police, Jack Ruby was
heard to shout:

00:24:42.950 --> 00:24:44.280
“You guys couldn’t do it.

00:24:44.280 --> 00:24:45.290
I did it for you.

00:24:45.290 --> 00:24:48.040
I had to show that a Jew has guts.

00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:50.400
I’m happy that I got him.”

00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:55.440
Less than two hours later, at 1:07pm, Lee
Harvey Oswald was pronounced dead.

00:24:55.440 --> 00:24:58.020
And that’s really the end of our story.

00:24:58.020 --> 00:25:01.870
There’s simply no time here to go into the
endless theories that grew in the wake of

00:25:01.870 --> 00:25:05.650
Oswald’s own assassination, linking him
to the mafia, to the Cubans, to the Soviets,

00:25:05.650 --> 00:25:07.150
to the CIA.

00:25:07.150 --> 00:25:09.630
No time for the Warren Commission.

00:25:09.630 --> 00:25:14.900
No time even to check back in with Jack Ruby,
dying of cancer complications in his cell

00:25:14.900 --> 00:25:18.940
on January 3, 1967, remorseless to the end.

00:25:18.940 --> 00:25:22.260
Perhaps the only thing we should mention is
the little green book Secret Service agent

00:25:22.260 --> 00:25:24.610
Mike Howard found in Oswald’s apartment.

00:25:24.610 --> 00:25:29.330
The one with a kill list written in it and
Governor Connally’s name decorated with

00:25:29.330 --> 00:25:30.330
daggers.

00:25:30.330 --> 00:25:32.990
Of Kennedy’s name, there was no sign.

00:25:32.990 --> 00:25:36.530
But even this is just a distraction from our
main narrative.

00:25:36.530 --> 00:25:39.740
There are plenty of videos on the JFK assassination
out there, millions.

00:25:39.740 --> 00:25:44.200
If you want theories on who did what and why,
they’re only a click away.

00:25:44.200 --> 00:25:49.850
But our job today was to tell the story not
of the conspiracy, but of the man at the heart

00:25:49.850 --> 00:25:50.850
of it.

00:25:50.850 --> 00:25:52.620
That job is now done.

00:25:52.620 --> 00:25:57.280
Lee Harvey Oswald was laid to rest at Rose
Hill Burial Park, Fort Worth, on November

00:25:57.280 --> 00:26:04.060
25, 1963, the exact same day John F Kennedy
was interred at Arlington Cemetery.

00:26:04.060 --> 00:26:25.890
Finally, after 24 years of rootless searching,
Oswald had at last found his home.

